Watch | Nagpur, Maharashtra: RSS chief Mohan Bhagwat says, "The recent devastating tragedy in Nepal and the incident in Kolkata have both caused deep sorrow. However, the Kolkata incident cannot be blamed on nature; the responsibility lies with the stampede and the way the crowd surged. Our sympathies are with the victims there as well, and efforts are underway to provide relief and assistance. As for the disaster in Nepal, why did it happen? The Himalayan region extends across several countries in today’s geographical map, including India, Tibet, Bhutan, and China. The pursuit of one-sided development in these regions has led to ecological instability across the Himalayas. Although technology and science have advanced, the large-scale loss of human lives remains deeply distressing. We offer our condolences and must participate in relief efforts, as we should. However, the fundamental solution lies in developing a comprehensive and balanced vision of development,  one that takes everyone along, remains sustainable in the long run, and does not become so costly that the very people it is meant to benefit cannot survive. We must relearn the principles of development that ensure progress without endangering human life and the natural environment..."

@RSSorg | @DrMohanBhagwat 

(Source: RSS / X)

